        {
          "title": "A Systematic Evaluation of Large Language Models for PTSD Severity Estimation: The Role of Contextual Knowledge and Modeling Strategies",
          "title_zh": "大语言模型用于 PTSD 严重程度估计的系统评估：上下文知识与建模策略的作用",
          "url": "http://arxiv.org/abs/2602.06015v2",
          "source": "arXiv",
          "section": "research_papers",
          "organization": "DeepSeek",
          "language": "en",
          "arxiv_id": "2602.06015",
          "summary": "The study evaluates 11 LLMs on narratives and self-reported PTSD severity from 1,437 individuals, varying contextual knowledge such as subscale definitions, distribution summaries and interview questions, plus modeling strategies. It finds detailed construct definitions and more reasoning effort improve accuracy, open-weight models plateau beyond 70B while newer closed models improve, and ensembling a supervised model with zero-shot LLMs performs best.",
