        {
          "title": "Generics in science communication: Misaligned interpretations across laypeople, scientists, and large language models",
          "title_zh": "科学传播中的泛指表达：外行、科学家与大语言模型之间的解读错位",
          "url": "http://arxiv.org/abs/2602.06190v1",
          "source": "arXiv",
          "section": "research_papers",
          "organization": "DeepSeek",
          "language": "en",
          "arxiv_id": "2602.06190",
          "summary": "The study compares how laypeople, scientists and two LLMs, ChatGPT-5 and DeepSeek, interpret generic statements used to communicate research findings. Laypeople judged scientific generics as more generalizable and credible than most scientists did, and the LLMs rated them even higher, highlighting risks of overgeneralization in human- and LLM-mediated science communication.",
