        {
          "title": "REBEL: Hidden Knowledge Recovery via Evolutionary-Based Evaluation Loop",
          "title_zh": "REBEL：通过进化式评估循环恢复隐藏知识",
          "url": "http://arxiv.org/abs/2602.06248v1",
          "source": "arXiv",
          "section": "research_papers",
          "organization": "",
          "language": "en",
          "arxiv_id": "2602.06248",
          "summary": "REBEL uses an evolutionary loop to generate adversarial prompts that probe whether supposedly unlearned data can still be recovered from LLMs. On subsets of TOFU and WMDP it reports attack success rates up to 60% and 93%, outperforming static baselines and suggesting current unlearning methods may offer only superficial protection.",
